## Strict bounded profile

**EAGER validates every discovered pack/idx envelope, CRC, frame, delta and
reconstructed object hash before any success**, including metadata-only and
loose-selected queries. This is stricter than ordinary queries, not full fsck
of all unselected loose objects. Verified bodies are invocation-pinned with
no eviction; each physical representation retains verification/depth across
OID reuse. The original B10 eviction clause is out-of-profile, not a pass.

**Practical cumulative work can reject packs far below the nominal32MiB
per-pack cap.** Even the static necessary lower bound `W >= 4P-52` is
32,000,004 at P=8,000,014, exceeding32,000,000 before index/inflation/query
work. This is arithmetic, not a latency measurement or a fit guarantee. All24
fixed numbers remain unchanged in ROOT-ACCEPTANCE.json and the frozen limits
source: cumulative reads64MiB/inflation128MiB/work32m, live logical resident
64MiB, packs8×32MiB, intrinsic delta depth32, plus the other declared caps.
No override, new budget, refund or provider guarantee follows from acceptance.

Storage remains SHA1 loose objects, directory/bare repositories, DIRC2/3 and
pack2/3+idx2. Promisor, alternates, shallow/replace/graft/reftable, gitfiles,
linked worktrees/commondir and thin external bases refuse. Only the exact
inert-sidecar allowlist is admitted, regular/no-follow and<=16MiB; membership/
type/size/available-stat observations do not establish sidecar body integrity.

Configuration remains the finite key/value families of frozen config.ts:
repository format0/bare-layout agreement/filemode handling; fixed true/false
case/conversion/rename controls; eol=lf, abbrev7, context3; inert declared user,
remote and branch metadata. Unsupported includes/routing/conversion/settings
refuse. No ambient global configuration, hooks, filters, host execution or
network. API options remain replace/discoveryBoundary only.

The module is read-only: no Git write commands or rename detection. Metadata
and path links refuse; tracked symlink text is not followed. Text patches are
bounded strictUTF8 without NUL; raw blob/names/quiet byte paths remain separate.
Observed namespace/content checks are not atomic snapshots or ABA guarantees;
provider atime may change. Applicable virtual hunks are not native hunk-choice
parity. Opaque provider/native work is not forcibly preempted.

